# Struct allowlist for the agentd SDK surface.
#
# One Go struct name per line. Lines starting with `#` and blank
# lines are ignored. The text after `#` on each entry line is a
# short rationale / skip reason — it is parsed as a comment, not
# structure.
#
# Drift detector: `scripts/regen-agentd.py`.
#
# Status conventions:
#   PORTED   — Go struct has a TypeScript mirror in src/agentd/
#   SKIP     — intentionally not ported (rationale required)
#
# When adding a new Go struct under agentd/internal/**, either port
# it (then add it here as PORTED) or list it as SKIP with a reason.
# Unlisted structs are reported as drift by regen-agentd.py.

# ── PORTED (TypeScript mirror exists in src/agentd/) ──
AgentCgroupStat   # PORTED → node.ts
AgentConfig       # PORTED → paths.ts
BotCapabilities   # PORTED → paths.ts
BotSource         # PORTED → paths.ts
HealthResponse    # PORTED → paths.ts
KeyFact           # PORTED → paths.ts
L0Rule            # PORTED → security.ts (TS wins: l0-engine.ts is fuller)
L1Result          # PORTED → security.ts as L1ScoreResult
Memory            # PORTED → paths.ts
Message           # PORTED → paths.ts
SandboxMeta       # PORTED → sandbox.ts
Session           # PORTED → paths.ts
Task              # PORTED → paths.ts
ToolCall          # PORTED → paths.ts (OpenAI tool-calling assistant turn)
ToolCallFunction  # PORTED → paths.ts
ToolDef           # PORTED → paths.ts (OpenAI tools-field definition)
ToolDefFunction   # PORTED → paths.ts
ToolDefinition    # PORTED → tools.ts (MinUserType field omitted, daemon-only)
ToolExecRequest   # PORTED → tools.ts
ToolExecResponse  # PORTED → tools.ts
ToolResult        # PORTED → tools.ts

# ── SKIP (intentionally not ported — rationale) ──
AgentStat             # SKIP — daemon-internal stats record, superseded by AgentCgroupStat on the wire
BotCapabilitiesResponse  # SKIP — Web-tier route response wrapper, lives under lib/extra/agent/ on TS side
Collector             # SKIP — Go implementation type (metrics collector), not wire
Decision              # SKIP — clawless-side per-task summary struct; clashes name with the Web's L2 Decision (security.ts). Web Decision is authoritative; this struct is a task-summary shape.
ExecResult            # SKIP — sandbox-internal provider return type (not exposed over HTTP; HTTP path uses ToolExecResponse/ToolResult)
GitInfo               # SKIP — completion-notification-only struct, not part of the tool protocol surface
KnowledgeSearchResult # SKIP — RAG result type; lives under lib/core/knowledge on TS side
L1Client              # SKIP — Go HTTP client implementation, not wire
LLMProxyRequest       # SKIP — proxy-internal. Now carries a Tools field for native tool calling (P9) + ToolChoice for constraining parallel calls (P10 review fix), but still not part of the external tool protocol; the SDK surface is the Message/ToolCall/ToolDef shapes it transports, not the envelope.
Manager               # SKIP — Go daemon singleton, not wire
Mount                 # SKIP — SandboxSpec sub-field, daemon-internal config
Notification          # SKIP — Web-tier Notification schema (lib/extra/agent) is authoritative
NotificationSendResponse  # SKIP — Web-tier response wrapper
ReviewLog             # SKIP — persisted audit row, not part of the tool protocol surface
Sandbox               # SKIP — SandboxMeta is the wire shape; `Sandbox` is the daemon-internal struct
SandboxSpec           # SKIP — daemon-internal sandbox creation config (TOML/runtime knobs)
Server                # SKIP — Go HTTP server struct, not wire
TaskMemoryRequest     # SKIP — Web-tier post-task memory extraction request, not tool protocol
TaskSummary           # SKIP — Web-tier long-running task state, mirrored from TS already
ToolActivityLog       # SKIP — persisted audit row, not part of the tool protocol surface
ToolRegistry          # SKIP — Go daemon registry implementation, not wire
UploadResult          # SKIP — Web-tier blob-upload response, lives under lib/core/blob on TS side
ProjectSandbox        # SKIP — Web-tier organization-unit row, not part of the tool protocol (renamed from Workspace; Go keeps a deprecated Workspace alias)
